<section class="cc26-pagehero cc26-pagehero--image cc26-pagehero--dim" style="--hero-img: url('/assets/img/services-consign.jpg')">
    <div class="cc26-wrap cc26-pagehero__in">
        <div class="cc26-eyebrow">Consignment</div>
        <h1>Consign with Tony, not the auction house.</h1>
        <p class="cc26-lede">For coins worth $2,000 and up, Cabbage Coins sells on your behalf on our website, at coin shows and across our network of collectors. The commission is lower, no buyer's fee is taken out of your price, and you're paid within 3 days of the sale.</p>
        <div class="cc26-hero__ctas">
            <a class="cc26-btn cc26-btn--gold cc26-btn--lg" href="#calculator">Compare your payout</a>
            <button type="button" class="cc26-textlink cs-linkbtn" data-modal-open="cc26-contact">Or ask Tony about consigning</button>
        </div>
    </div>
</section>

{# ---------- Consignment Program ---------- #}
<section class="cc26-wrap cc26-section" id="consign">
    <article class="cc26-service">
        <img class="cc26-service__img" src="/assets/img/services-auction.jpg" alt="Tony inspecting a coin with a loupe at a show table" loading="lazy" width="1400" height="1050" style="object-position: 40% 50%">
        <div class="cc26-service__body">
            <span class="cc26-badge">By application only</span>
            <h2>Consignment Program</h2>
            <p class="cc26-service__lede">Cabbage Coins handles the whole sale for you, from photography to the show floor. You keep ownership until your coin sells.</p>
            <div class="cc26-tiers">
                <div class="cc26-tier cc26-tier--list">
                    <div class="cc26-tier__copy">
                        <h3>What's included</h3>
                        <ul class="cc26-checks">
                            <li>Professional photography of each coin</li>
                            <li>Publication on the Cabbage Coins website</li>
                            <li>Display and active selling at regional and national coin shows</li>
                            <li>Option for a dedicated collection webpage <em>(e.g. “The XYZ Mercury Dime Collection”)</em> or integration into the existing inventory</li>
                            <li>Agreed-upon pricing in writing before any publication or display</li>
                            <li>Paid within 3 days of the sale: cash, check, Zelle, PayPal, Venmo, or however you prefer</li>
                        </ul>
                    </div>
                </div>
                <div class="cc26-tier cc26-tier--list">
                    <div class="cc26-tier__copy">
                        <h3>Commission</h3>
                        <p>No upfront fees. You pay a commission only when your coin sells, and the rate drops as the coin's value rises. The minimum is $2,000 per coin.</p>
                        <table class="cs-rates">
                            <thead><tr><th scope="col">Sale price</th><th scope="col">Commission</th></tr></thead>
                            <tbody>
                                <tr><td>$2,000 – $5,000</td><td>10%</td></tr>
                                <tr><td>$5,001 – $10,000</td><td>8%</td></tr>
                                <tr><td>$10,001 – $15,000</td><td>7%</td></tr>
                                <tr><td>$15,001 – $25,000</td><td>6%</td></tr>
                                <tr><td>$25,001 – $50,000</td><td>5%</td></tr>
                                <tr><td>Over $50,000</td><td>3%</td></tr>
                            </tbody>
                        </table>
                        <p class="cc26-tier__note">The rate is set by each coin's final sale price and applies to the whole price. Coins under $2,000? We'd rather <a href="/selltous/">make you an offer</a> and buy them outright.</p>
                    </div>
                </div>
            </div>
        </div>
    </article>
</section>

{# ---------- Calculator ---------- #}
<section class="cc26-wrap cc26-section" id="calculator">
    <div class="cs-calc">
        <div class="cs-calc__head">
            <div class="cc26-eyebrow">Consign or auction?</div>
            <h2 class="cc26-h2">See what you'd take home.</h2>
            <p class="cc26-muted">At auction, bidders know they'll pay a buyer's fee on top of the hammer price, so they bid lower to cover it. In effect that fee comes out of your coin's price. Enter your numbers to compare.</p>
        </div>

        <form class="cs-calc__in cc26-form" onsubmit="return false" novalidate>
            <label for="cs-value">What is your coin worth?
                <span class="cs-money"><span>$</span><input type="text" id="cs-value" inputmode="decimal" autocomplete="off" placeholder="10,000"></span>
                <small>Your estimate of what a buyer would pay for it.</small>
            </label>

            <fieldset class="cs-fee">
                <legend>The auction's buyer's fee</legend>
                <div class="cs-fee__opts" role="radiogroup" aria-label="Buyer's fee">
                    <button type="button" class="cs-pill" data-fee="20" aria-pressed="false">20%</button>
                    <button type="button" class="cs-pill" data-fee="22" aria-pressed="false">22%</button>
                    <button type="button" class="cs-pill" data-fee="22.5" aria-pressed="false">22.5%</button>
                    <button type="button" class="cs-pill" data-fee="25" aria-pressed="false">25%</button>
                    <span class="cs-pct"><input type="text" id="cs-fee" inputmode="decimal" autocomplete="off" placeholder="Other" aria-label="Other buyer's fee percent"><span>%</span></span>
                </div>
                <small>Check the auction's terms of sale for its buyer's fee (sometimes called the buyer's premium).</small>
            </fieldset>

            <label for="cs-other">Other auction charges (optional)
                <span class="cs-money"><span>$</span><input type="text" id="cs-other" inputmode="decimal" autocomplete="off" placeholder="0"></span>
                <small>For example: a seller's commission, photo or lot fees, or shipping and insurance to the auction.</small>
            </label>
        </form>

        <div class="cs-calc__out" aria-live="polite">
            <p class="cs-empty">Enter your coin's value and pick a buyer's fee to see the comparison.</p>
            <p class="cs-small" hidden>Coins under $2,000 aren't eligible for consignment. We'd rather buy them outright: <a href="/selltous/">get an offer from Tony</a>.</p>

            <div class="cs-results" hidden>
                <div class="cs-card cs-card--us">
                    <div class="cc26-eyebrow">Consign with Cabbage Coins</div>
                    <div class="cs-card__net" data-out="usNet"></div>
                    <dl>
                        <div><dt>Sale price</dt><dd data-out="usPrice"></dd></div>
                        <div><dt>Commission (<span data-out="usRate"></span>)</dt><dd data-out="usFee"></dd></div>
                    </dl>
                    <p class="cs-card__time"><strong>Paid within 3 days</strong> of the sale, however you prefer.</p>
                </div>
                <div class="cs-card">
                    <div class="cc26-eyebrow">Auction</div>
                    <div class="cs-card__net" data-out="auNet"></div>
                    <dl>
                        <div><dt>Est. hammer price*</dt><dd data-out="auHammer"></dd></div>
                        <div><dt>Buyer's fee (<span data-out="auRate"></span>), paid by the winner</dt><dd data-out="auBp"></dd></div>
                        <div data-row="other"><dt>Other charges</dt><dd data-out="auOther"></dd></div>
                    </dl>
                    <p class="cs-card__time"><strong>Paid about 45 days after the auction closes</strong>, and the sale itself is often weeks or months after you consign.**</p>
                </div>
                <div class="cs-diff" data-out="diff"></div>
            </div>

            <p class="cs-foot">* Estimate: assumes the winning bidder pays your coin's value in total, so the hammer price is that value minus the buyer's fee. Real results vary with every coin and sale.<br>** Typical of major coin auctions; check your auction's consignment agreement for its exact settlement terms.</p>
        </div>
    </div>
</section>

